:"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-paquetes","content":"Un `Paquete` define el significado de los bytes; un `Buffer` proporciona el espacio y las operaciones para escribirlos."},"2407":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-36","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-tnet","content":"`Buffer` es la evolución renombrada de `TNBuffer`. La arquitectura de pool, lectura/escritura y reciclado procede de TNet, mientras que la nomenclatura de Eco es la API utilizada por Pandora."},"2408":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-37","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-tnet","content":"Implementación del buffer binario."},"2409":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers-38","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte/buffers#relación-con-tnet","content":"Repositorio upstream."},"2410":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","type":"page","content":"Transporte","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Red","Red","Contenido","Transporte"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte"},"2411":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte-0","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","content":"Cómo Eco convierte operaciones en paquetes, las serializa y las transporta entre cliente y servidor."},"2412":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte-1","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte#transporte","content":"Transporte"},"2413":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte-2","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/transporte#flujo-completo","content":"Flujo completo"},"2414":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte-3","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/transporte","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/r